### Page contents

| Section | Coverage |
|---------|----------|
| **Purpose** | One primary (`btn-forge` / `btn-primary`) per hero, modal, or sticky-footer region; PDCA workflow |
| **Passing signals** | Canonical KS hero stack: one `btn-forge`, optional `btn-cyan-outline`, `landing-hero-secondary-link` |
| **Failing signals** | Multiple filled primaries; modal/sticky-footer duplicates; distinction from `DET.BUTTON.GROUP.MAX` |
| **Before example** | Two `btn-forge` links in `.landing-hero-actions__buttons` inside `.landing-hero-wide` |
| **After example** | One `btn-forge` + `btn-cyan-outline` + `landing-hero-secondary-links` row |
| **Evidence and remediation** | `metrics.ctaHierarchyReport`, severity tiers, six-step fix order |
| **Related rules** | `DET.BUTTON.GROUP.MAX`, `DET.CTA.LABEL_NONEMPTY`, `DET.CONTEXT.BURDEN`, `DET.CARD.ACTION_LIMIT`, `AI.VISUAL.HIERARCHY` |

### Real KS classes used

